# Design Patterns for gRPC Server

## Repository Pattern
- Separate data access logic from business logic
- Create `internal/repository/` for all data operations
- Use interfaces to allow switching between different storage backends

```go
type UserRepository interface {
    Create(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error
    GetByID(ctx context.Context, id string) (*domain.User, error)
    Update(ctx context.Context, user *domain.User) error
    Delete(ctx context.Context, id string) error
}
```

## Factory Pattern
- Use for creating different types of repositories or services
- Useful for configuration-based service instantiation

```go
type ServiceFactory interface {
    CreateUserService() UserService
    CreateOrderService() OrderService
}
```

## Strategy Pattern
- Implement different validation strategies
- Different authentication methods
- Multiple storage backends

```go
type ValidationStrategy interface {
    Validate(user *domain.User) error
}
```

## Observer Pattern
- Event-driven architecture for service communication
- Useful for audit logging, notifications

```go
type EventPublisher interface {
    Publish(event domain.Event) error
}
```

## Decorator Pattern
- Add cross-cutting concerns without modifying core logic
- Logging, metrics, authentication, rate limiting

```go
type LoggingUserService struct {
    UserService
    logger Logger
}
```

## Command Pattern
- Encapsulate gRPC requests as commands
- Useful for request validation and processing pipelines

```go
type Command interface {
    Execute(ctx context.Context) error
    Validate() error
}
```

## Adapter Pattern
- Convert between gRPC protobuf and domain models
- Integration with external services

```go
type UserAdapter interface {
    ToProto(user *domain.User) *pb.User
    FromProto(pbUser *pb.User) *domain.User
}
```

## Chain of Responsibility Pattern
- Request processing pipelines
- Middleware chains for authentication, validation, logging

```go
type Middleware interface {
    Process(ctx context.Context, req interface{}) (interface{}, error)
    SetNext(middleware Middleware)
}
```

## Singleton Pattern
- Configuration management
- Database connections
- Logger instances

```go
type Config struct {
    Port string
    Database DatabaseConfig
}

var once sync.Once
var config *Config

func GetConfig() *Config {
    once.Do(func() {
        config = loadConfig()
    })
    return config
}
```

## Builder Pattern
- Complex server configuration
- gRPC server setup with multiple services

```go
type ServerBuilder interface {
    WithPort(port string) ServerBuilder
    WithService(service interface{}) ServerBuilder
    WithInterceptor(interceptor grpc.UnaryServerInterceptor) ServerBuilder
    Build() *grpc.Server
}
```
